h1, p , div-non semmatic tags
differnce bteween html4 and html 5





structure of html:
<!DOCTYPE html> - qrick mode
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Document</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Im h1</h1>
    
</body>
</html>

<!DOCTYPE html>- declare the document type as html5
<html> root elemnet

<head> meta tags and title
<meta> meta tags contains meta data
meta data-information that describes  other data.

UTF-8- Unicode transformation format
<body> contains visble content of the webpages , such as text, images and other elemnets


To run the html we need .html and live server, you can download it from your extensions..
and click on the live serever and then your first page is displayed in the browser then 
The browser receives the HTML document and its built-in HTML parser parses the markup. <!DOCTYPE html> tells the browser to use standards mode, and then the parser processes elements such as <html>, <head>, <body>, <h1>, etc., and constructs the DOM.”

 Core Components - Main/building blocks to build a webpage
Tags- These are prdefined keyword
      These have some meaning and builtin props to be displayed on the webpage.
      to structure the webpages



      synatx: <tagname> </tagname>
      examples <p></p>



      Types of tags- Paired tags/container tags -<p></p><h1></h1>
                    self-closing tags/void tags/single- <img/>,<hr>,<br>,<meta>
                     Heading tags -h1 to h6
                    structured tags- article,dic,section
                    Formatting tags - bold,italit,em
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Atributes- Which gives additonal information
        height, width, style, class, id, src,alt, href


        synatx:
        <tagName attributeName = "AttributeValue"> Content </tagName>



           Types
           element specific-  href, alt,src,type
           Global- id,class,style,height,width,title
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
               
Elements-  Tags+content or Tags+Content+attributes
   syntax:<tagname> content </tagname>
            types of elements
            -block - These are the elemnts lawsy diplays in a nwline
                     occupies the entire row
            -inline- These are the elemnsts displayed on the same line
                     height and width are not applicable
                     occupies how much space it requires
                    <img> <b> <button></button> <input>
            inline-block - converting inline elemnt to block
            Inline you can apply height,width,margin left and right
            But Img is alose an inline still we can apply height and width since it has inbuilt option,
                           elmens are displayed on a newline but they ca be used as a inline elemnts


    Golden rules
    Never write a block line inside Inline elemnts
       <b>Im the boldest and <p>Im the para inside the inline{b}</p></b>
            







